# UW-Madison GI Tract Image Segmentation — solution

Task: 2D MRI segmentation of 3 organs (`large_bowel`, `small_bowel`, `stomach`), evaluated by
`0.4 * Dice + 0.6 * (1 - normalized 3D Hausdorff)` (metric `dice-hausdorff-combo`, higher is better).
Submission: RLE-encoded masks in `submission.csv` (`id,class,predicted`).

## Data format (verified empirically)
- Inputs: 16-bit grayscale PNG, `slice_<idx>_<W>_<H>_<sx>_<sy>.png` (filename order is **W,H**).
- `train.csv` RLE is **row-major (C-order)**: `mask = flat.reshape(H, W)`; encoding uses `mask.reshape(-1)`.
  (The TASK.md wording says column-major but this is contradicted by direct image/mask overlay checks.)
- Masks are multi-label per class (3 independent sigmoids).

## Pipeline
1. `code/build_manifest.py`: map every `id` (case_day_slice) to its image path and true `(H,W)`,
   group by `case_day`, build z-neighbours.
2. `code/common.py`: dataset (2.5D input = slices `z-1,z,z+1`, per-image 1–99 percentile normalization),
   RLE encode/decode (row-major), augmentation (flips, rot90, shift/scale/rotate, brightness/contrast).
3. `code/train.py`: `segmentation_models_pytorch` Unet + ImageNet encoder, BCEWithLogits + Dice loss,
   AdamW, 1-epoch warmup + cosine LR, gradient clipping, AMP. Validation = group K-fold by `case_day`
   (fold file from the swarm: `blackboard/betelgeuse_zeta_folds.csv`). Best checkpoint by positive-slice Dice.
4. `code/infer.py`: test-time augmentation (identity, hflip, vflip, rot180), saves per-slice class
   probabilities `[N,3,S,S]` float16.
5. `code/make_submission.py`: per-class threshold, 3x3 closing, connected-component min-area filter,
   upsample probability mask to the original `(H,W)`, row-major RLE.
6. `code/handoff.py` / ensemble: probabilities from all agents are aligned by `id`, blended, then the
   tuned threshold/CC recipe (selected on fold-0 OOF with `code/simlib.py` metric) is applied.

## Validation
Group K-fold by `case_day` (test case-days are disjoint from train; 19/28 test cases share a patient
with train but on different days). Local metric: `code/simlib.py` implements row-major RLE, 2D Dice
(both-empty = 1), 3D symmetric Hausdorff normalized by `sqrt(H^2+W^2)`, combined as in the task.

## External models (all ImageNet-pretrained backbones, no competition-specific data)
| model | source | purpose | license |
|---|---|---|---|
| `efficientnet_b3` (timm) via `segmentation_models_pytorch` `Unet`, `encoder_weights='imagenet'` | https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models (timm 0.9.7) / https://github.com/qubvel/segmentation_models_pytorch | encoder initialization | Apache-2.0 |
| `resnet34` (torchvision/timm) via smp `Unet` (early baseline, superseded) | torchvision 0.17.0 | encoder initialization | BSD-3-Clause |

Only general ImageNet weights were used; no competition solution/checkpoint or test labels were used.

## Final submission
`submission.csv` is the swarm's best validated ensemble. See the blackboard messages for the exact
model lists, ensemble weights and postprocessing recipe.
EOF
